{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":true,"decision":"pass","reasons":[],"slug":"canva-designs","displayName":"Canva","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/hith3sh/skills/canva-designs","publisherHandle":"hith3sh","publisherDisplayName":"Jay","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/hith3sh","version":"1.0.6","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1780988699481,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/canva-designs/card?ownerHandle=hith3sh&version=1.0.6","sha256":"3197724d201689db14bb11e1147264f72bccf9b1d3c41421d6b8dbe3fb291069","size":2444,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"c11242c8e8fe3e82b04da5edc252da7d3ff6fe3ac29e9ae976ecf255f868adad","bundleFingerprints":["ae074f22c98497015e1dd92ccdeccb58487b8efa53ec151b84ebc2dfb2fde776","989e55ca78206ab1a5ce64dc73f83e151f476b838d0b90dd390bc2d7a3244029"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":11195,"sha256":"b48d929c79a07cd9f75eb047bb781444bb80a8d9ce4e5fef0d29449c9e3e0ec1","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"clean","passed":true,"rawStatus":"clean","verdict":"benign","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a disclosed Canva integration that relies on the ClawLink plugin and OAuth, with no hidden or malicious behavior found.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789546865623,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unpinned Privileged Third-Party Plugin Installation"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":54,"endLine":58}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"334ca9514a83ae4b"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md`, lines 14, 54–58, 73–80, and 111–112  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unpinned third-party dependency with privileged OAuth-mediated access  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\nThe skill instructs the agent to install and explicitly allowlist a third-party plugin without pinning an immutable version or integrity hash:\n\n```markdown\nThis skill uses [ClawLink](https://claw-link.dev/?utm_source=clawhub&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_content=canva-designs) for hosted connection flows and credentials so you do not need to configure Canva API access yourself.\n```\n\n```bash\nopenclaw plugins install clawhub:clawlink-plugin\nopenclaw config set tools.alsoAllow '[\"clawlink-plugin\"]' --strict-json\nopenclaw gateway restart\n```\n\nThe installed component is then entrusted with OAuth credentials and authenticated API requests:\n\n```markdown\nAll Canva tool calls are authenticated automatically by ClawLink using the user's connected Canva account.\n\n**No API key is required in chat.** ClawLink stores the OAuth token securely and injects it into every Canva API request on the user's behalf.\n```\n\nThe effective tool interface is also obtained dynamically:\n\n```markdown\nTools are available dynamically from the live ClawLink catalog. Call `clawlink_list_tools --integration canva` to see the full list.\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe installation command identifies the plugin only as `clawhub:clawlink-plugin`; it does not specify a fixed version, immutable package digest, signature requirement, or checksum. The plugin is subsequently added to the tool allowlist and loaded by restarting the gateway.\n\nThis creates a supply-chain trust boundary that is not fully represented by the auditable project contents. The installed plugin can participate in authenticated Canva operations, while the remotely supplied live catalog determines which tools are exposed. Although the document describes ClawLink as verified and states that tokens are stored securely, the project contains no plugin implementation, lockfile, digest, signature metadata, or other local evidence with which to verify those claims.\n\nExploitation requires compromise, malicious replacement, or unauthorized modification of the plugin distribution or its update path. The documentation itself does not contain a malicious payload, and no evidence establishes that the current plugin is malicious.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker compromises the plugin publisher, registry account, package repository, distribution infrastructure, or another component capable of replacing the package resolved by `clawhub:clawlink-plugin`.\n2. Because the installation is not pinned to an immutable version or digest, the installation command resolves and downloads the attacker-controlled release.\n3. The configuration command explicitly allowlists the plugin.\n4. The gateway restart loads the compromised component into OpenClaw.\n5. The user pairs ClawLink and authorizes access to a Canva account.\n6. Authenticated Canva requests and OAuth-mediated operations pass through the compromised component.\n7. The component can inspect or alter proxied data and requests, or expose unexpected behavior through the dynamic tool interface, subject to its runtime permissions and the Canva OAuth scopes granted by the user.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nA successful supply-chain compromise could affect the connected Canva account and any locally accessible resources granted to the plugin runtime. Potential impact includes:\n\n- Unauthorized access to Canva designs, assets, exports, templates, or profile information within the granted OAuth scopes.\n- Disclosure or misuse of OAuth tokens if the compromised component can access token material.\n- Modification of authenticated Canva requests or returned data.\n- Exposure of additional or altered tools through the dynamic catalog.\n- Team-wide effects where the connected account is permitted to manage shared brand templates or assets.\n- Local impact within the plugin's OpenClaw permissions after it has been allowlisted and loaded.\n\nThe exact privileges cannot be determined from `SKILL.md`; they depend on the plugin runtime permissions and Canva scopes granted during authorization.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Pin the plugin to a reviewed, immutable version rather than installing a floating package identifier.\n2. Verify the package using a cryptographic digest and publisher signature before installation.\n3. Publish or reference reproducible, reviewable source code for the exact plugin release.\n4. Document the plugin's local permissions, network destinations, OAuth scopes, token-storage model, and update behavior.\n5. Request only the minimum Canva OAuth scopes needed for the user's requested operation.\n6. Require explicit, informed user approval before installing the plugin, changing the tool allowlist, restarting the gateway, or initiating OAuth delegation.\n7. Avoid automatically completing installation and restart steps merely because the skill was invoked.\n8. Constrain the dynamic tool catalog to an approved set of Canva operations and reject newly introduced tools until reviewed.\n9. Isolate the plugin with least-privilege filesystem, process, and network permissions.\n10. Provide a revocation procedure covering Canva authorization, ClawLink pairing, plugin removal, and token invalidation.\n11. Record and surface the exact plugin version and integrity metadata in audit logs.\n12. Re-review the plugin and its exposed tool catalog before accepting updates."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":75,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789546802.0135303,"endTime":1789546840.3451154}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"canva-designs","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57069y3ptcw14vthwejh66rrs8egwna-T7QwtZ/clawscan-skillspector-712198617/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-16T08:20:00.666667+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"NONE"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":252,"executable":false,"size_bytes":11195,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":false,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":4545,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":4559},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":4591,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":4605},{"node":"semantic_security_discovery","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":4123,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":4137}],"filtering_mode":"heuristic","llm_calls_attempted":3,"llm_calls_succeeded":3},"execution_successful":true,"analysis_completeness":{"total_components":1,"scanned_components":1,"coverage_percent":100,"is_complete":false,"status":"partial","execution_successful":true,"fully_inspected_files":1,"partially_inspected_files":0,"entirely_uninspected_files":0,"ledger_exceptions":[{"outcome":"partial","phase":"reference_resolution","reason_code":"reference_unresolved","message":"A local path-like reference could not be resolved unambiguously.","path":"SKILL.md","start_line":149,"end_line":149,"fatal":false},{"outcome":"partial","phase":"reference_resolution","reason_code":"reference_unresolved","message":"A local path-like reference could not be resolved unambiguously.","path":"SKILL.m